# Android services stubbed out on surya (POCO X3 NFC) because they only spam the
# journal under LuneOS/Halium (see meta-android's pre-start.d/50-stub-services).
#
# Justified from a logcat taken on the device on 2026-09-26, not copied from
# another port's list. Paths checked against the actual images in
# ~/webos/LuneOS/staging/surya-staging - a path that does not exist stubs
# nothing and says nothing.

# LineageOS display post-processing HAL. It SIGABRTs on startup, every time:
#
#   vendor.lineage.livedisplay@2.0-impl-sdm: PictureAdjustment backend not ready, exiting.
#   libc: Fatal signal 6 (SIGABRT) in tid 570 (vendor.lineage.)
#   DEBUG: Abort message: 'PictureAdjustment backend not ready, exiting.'
#
# The backend it wants is SDM's picture-adjustment interface, reached through a
# framework path that does not exist under Halium. init restarts it, so the
# crash repeats and each one writes a tombstone. It is LineageOS's colour and
# reading-mode tuning - nothing in LuneOS consumes it, so stubbing removes no
# capability. Binary confirmed present at this path in vendor.img.
vendor/bin/hw/vendor.lineage.livedisplay@2.1-service.surya

#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT stubbed: minimedia, and NOT the cause of the hwservicemanager loop.
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# An earlier reading of the 2026-09-26 log blamed `minimedia` (pid 555) for the
# once-per-second ISensors polling, because it hosts
# android.frameworks.sensorservice@1.0::ISensorManager and its log goes quiet
# just as the polling starts. That was wrong twice over: CameraService is
# event-driven and logs nothing when idle, and it had just finished enumerating
# the cameras successfully (cameraId 0, 1, 21), so going quiet is what working
# looks like.
#
# The client is host-side: sensorfwd. sensorfw's HybrisBackend::getBackend()
# tries HybrisBackendBinderAidl::isSupported(), then
# HybrisBackendBinderHidl::isSupported(), five times with sleep(1) between
# rounds, then gives up - and systemd restarts it. That is exactly the cadence
# and the count in the log (195 rounds over four minutes is about 39 runs of
# five). Nothing inside the container logs anything because the caller is not in
# the container; only hwservicemanager reports the attempts.
#
# So do not stub minimedia. It would remove camera and video for a symptom it
# does not cause.
#
# The HIDL half can never succeed here: surya's Android-15 vendor ships only
# /vendor/bin/hw/android.hardware.sensors-service.multihal (checked in
# vendor.img - no @2.x HIDL service exists). The AIDL half is the one that has
# to work, and it looks up android.hardware.sensors.ISensors/default on
# /dev/binder through libgbinder - which the container's own servicemanager
# serves fine (log: "Caller(pid=403) Found
# android.hardware.sensors.ISensors/default in device VINTF manifest").
#
# That makes this a libgbinder servicemanager API-level problem, not a missing
# backend, and the gbinder ApiLevel handling in luneos-device-config was
# reworked on 2026-09-25 - AFTER the rootfs these logs came from
# (luneos-dev-image-halium-arm64 20260924122732). Rebuild the rootfs and retest
# before adding anything here for sensors.
